{\f1\fs28\b\cf6 10.  How to Deploy to the Pi\par}
\par
{\f2\fs22 # From the project folder on the Mac:\par
scp -r . pi@pislider.local:~/slider/\par
\par
# Or targeted:\par
scp app.py cinematic_engine.py pi@pislider.local:~/slider/\par
\par
# Restart the service on the Pi:\par
ssh pi@pislider.local "sudo systemctl restart pislider"\par}
\par
{\f0\fs22 The service file is }{\f2\fs20 pislider.service}{\f0\fs22 . There is also }{\f2\fs20 pislider-wake.service}{\f0\fs22  which handles the Pi\rquote s USB wake behaviour.\par}
\par

{\f1\fs28\b\cf6 11.  How to Run the Retime App (Mac only)\par}
\par
{\f0\fs22 Double-click }{\f2\fs20 PiSlider Retime.app}{\f0\fs22  in the project folder. On first launch, right-click 薔  Open to bypass Gatekeeper (it is not code-signed).\par}
\par
{\f0\fs22 Or from Terminal:\par}
{\f2\fs22   cd /Users/timothyfennell/Documents/slider\\ claud\\ code\par
  python3 retime_server.py\par}
\par
{\f0\fs22 Required Python packages (Mac): }{\f2\fs20 flask flask-cors scipy numpy}{\f0\fs22 . The app opens at }{\f2\fs20 http://localhost:9077}{\f0\fs22 .\par}
\par
{\f0\fs22 Workflow after generating the XML:\par
  1. Open DaVinci Resolve (free version is fine)\par
  2. File 薔  Import Timeline 薔  select the }{\f2\fs20 .xml}{\f0\fs22  file\par
  3. Select each retimed clip (tracks 2+)\par
  4. Inspector 薔  Retime and Scaling 薔  Retime Process 薔  Optical Flow\par
  5. Render\par}
\par

{\f1\fs28\b\cf6 12.  Tim\rquote s Working Style Notes\par}
\par
{\f0\fs22 \'95  Tim is highly technical across the full stack and does not need concepts explained. He appreciates concise, direct answers.\par
\'95  He often has the full context of why something was built a certain way and will push back if a suggestion conflicts with a constraint that isn\rquote t obvious from the code alone. Ask if unsure rather than assuming.\par
\'95  The project is a passion project. Correctness and elegance matter. He is willing to take time to do things right.\par
\'95  The retime pipeline was initially conceived around CSV files and image copying; Tim clarified that the data already lives in JSON and that Resolve should do the heavy interpolation work, leading to the speed-keyframe FCP7 XML approach. Always check whether existing data structures already cover a need before proposing new ones.\par
\'95  When a path is blocked (e.g. Resolve Studio required, Scripts menu not working), Tim will ask \ldblquote is there another way?\rdblquote  and expects a real alternative, not a workaround that has the same root problem.\par
\'95  Tim prefers code with minimal comments \emdash  only add a comment when the WHY is non-obvious.\par}
\par

